{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7aa7c8d497a34f4d","name":"card_event_uss_arcfish","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_uss_arcfish","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"USS ARCHERFISH","text":"Destroy a random enemy unit. Repeat if there is a Navy card on top of your deck.","flavorText":"USS Archerfish (SS-311) was a US Navy Balao-class submarine commissioned in 1943. The submarine is probably best known for sinking the Japanese aircraft carrier Shinano, which is the largest warship ever sunk by a submarine. Archerfish operated in the Pacific during WWII, conducting patrols, laying mines and gathering intelligence. On 29 November 1944, off the coast of Japan, Archerfish launched six torpedoes at Shinano, which had only recently been commissioned and was on her maiden voyage. Four torpedoes struck, and despite her massive size and protective design, the carrier capsized and sank a few hours later. This marked one of the most significant submarine victories of the war. Archerfish completed five war patrols and earned seven battle stars. After the war she served in various roles including sonar testing and Arctic missions, before being decommissioned in 1968.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.navy"],"Name":"card_event_uss_arcfish","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_uss_arcfish_title","SourceString":"USS ARCHERFISH","LocalizedString":"USS ARCHERFISH"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_uss_arcfish_text","SourceString":"Destroy a random enemy unit. Repeat if there is a Navy card on top of your deck.","LocalizedString":"Destroy a random enemy unit. Repeat if there is a Navy card on top of your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_uss_arcfish_history","SourceString":"USS Archerfish (SS-311) was a US Navy Balao-class submarine commissioned in 1943. The submarine is probably best known for sinking the Japanese aircraft carrier Shinano, which is the largest warship ever sunk by a submarine. Archerfish operated in the Pacific during WWII, conducting patrols, laying mines and gathering intelligence. On 29 November 1944, off the coast of Japan, Archerfish launched six torpedoes at Shinano, which had only recently been commissioned and was on her maiden voyage. Four torpedoes struck, and despite her massive size and protective design, the carrier capsized and sank a few hours later. This marked one of the most significant submarine victories of the war. Archerfish completed five war patrols and earned seven battle stars. After the war she served in various roles including sonar testing and Arctic missions, before being decommissioned in 1968.","LocalizedString":"USS Archerfish (SS-311) was a US Navy Balao-class submarine commissioned in 1943. The submarine is probably best known for sinking the Japanese aircraft carrier Shinano, which is the largest warship ever sunk by a submarine. Archerfish operated in the Pacific during WWII, conducting patrols, laying mines and gathering intelligence. On 29 November 1944, off the coast of Japan, Archerfish launched six torpedoes at Shinano, which had only recently been commissioned and was on her maiden voyage. Four torpedoes struck, and despite her massive size and protective design, the carrier capsized and sank a few hours later. This marked one of the most significant submarine victories of the war. Archerfish completed five war patrols and earned seven battle stars. After the war she served in various roles including sonar testing and Arctic missions, before being decommissioned in 1968."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAttacks"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'AU_Order_UBoat_04'","ObjectPa